From 6e7b0d4321f37b04f032db98a90c695c41a9191f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:38:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(xtask): seed a new worktree's target/ so solidcore is
 not compiled again

sccache hashes OUT_DIR and the cwd of a Rust compile. Both name the
worktree, so each build-script crate and each crate above it (solidcore,
flecs) missed the cache in a new worktree. Cargo's fingerprints do not
name the worktree.

Before its first step, the gate now copies the dependency units of the
checkout with the most units (registry and git packages only; never a
workspace member or a path dependency). It replaces units that cargo
xtask built just before, keeps the file times, takes cargo's locks
without a wait and passes over a busy checkout. CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 turns
it off.

Fixes #2575

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
